# (%tid.x − 32·⌊%tid.x/32⌋)·2^26 stays below 2^31 on all 1024 threads,
# and ptxas stores at param_0 plus it. The range of %tid.x taken with
# its own floor, x = 32·q + r, is that of 0·q + 2^26·r, so mul.lo.s32
# does not leave 32 bits and the address reads, 32 sectors per warp
# request; each term on its own would reach 1023·2^26.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/expanded_rem.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [67108864·%tid.x - 2147483648·⌊%tid.x/32⌋ + param_0] sectors/req 32 (ideal 4){{$}}
